// Flags raw PocketBase access that bypasses pbtsdb's store. A pbtsdb collection
// (from useStore()) is read with `useLiveQuery`/`useOrgLiveQuery` and mutated
// with `.insert()/.update()/.delete()` on the collection variable; the raw PB
// client is reached via `pb.collection('x')` and exposes `.create/.update/
// .delete` (writes) and `.getFullList/.getFirstListItem/.getOne/.getList`
// (reads). Matching the `.collection(...)` accessor with one of those methods
// catches the raw path without flagging pbtsdb usage.
//
// Why reads count too: a raw read always hits the network and ignores records
// the pbtsdb store may already hold (loaded by a mounted useLiveQuery, a prior
// read, or preload()). In a component/hook, read with useLiveQuery; in a
// non-React context (a mutationFn/queryFn callback, an imperative util), use
// readCollectionCached/findCollectionCached from
// @tinycld/core/lib/read-collection-cached, which reads through the store cache.
// Writes still go through a useMutation generator (@tinycld/core/lib/mutations).
//
// Legitimate exceptions (seed scripts, test fixtures) are excluded by the
// plugin's `includes` globs in biome.json. Per-site exceptions — a multipart
// FormData upload pbtsdb can't carry, a bootstrap read that seeds the store
// before it exists, deliberate server-side pagination — use an inline
// `// biome-ignore lint/plugin/pbtsdb-no-raw-pb-access: <why>` with the reason.
//
// See CLAUDE.md → "Data Queries & Mutations".
// Match the `.collection(...).method` member access itself (not `.method(args)`)
// so a call with a type argument — `pb.collection('x').getOne<T>(id)` — is still
// caught; the args-form pattern silently misses generic calls.
`$obj.collection($name).$method` where {
    $method <: or {
        `create`,
        `update`,
        `delete`,
        `getFullList`,
        `getFirstListItem`,
        `getOne`,
        `getList`
    },
    register_diagnostic(
        span = $method,
        message = "Raw PocketBase access via pb.collection(...) bypasses the pbtsdb store. Read with useLiveQuery (component/hook) or readCollectionCached (non-React); write with a useMutation generator from @tinycld/core/lib/mutations.",
        severity = "error"
    )
}
